📅 Day 30 – Console-Based JDBC Mini Project (Part 1)

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on starting a console-based mini project using JDBC. The mentor explained the objective of the project and how a Java console application can interact with a database to manage records.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Mini Project Introduction

The project aims to build a console-based database management system using Java and JDBC.

The application will allow users to interact with the database through the command line interface.

It will perform database operations such as inserting, retrieving, updating, and deleting records.

2️⃣ Project Structure

The mentor explained the basic structure required for the project:

Main Class → Handles user interaction and menu options

Database Connection Class → Establishes connection with the database

DAO Classes → Perform database operations

This structure helps maintain a clean and organized application design.

3️⃣ Database Connectivity Setup

During the practical session, I implemented the initial code to:

Establish a connection between the Java application and the database

Verify that the connection works correctly

Prepare the project for further database operations

This connection setup will be used later to perform various database operations through the console interface.